WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.368
-My first guest
is a world-renowned chef

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.569
and one
of my all-time favorites.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.172
He's also
an Emmy-nominated TV host.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:09.609
His show "Hell's Kitchen"
returns this Thursday

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.943
[British accent]
at 8:00 p.m. on Fox,

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.111
and you can see him!

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:13.445
[ Normal voice ] Sorry.
You can see him

00:00:13.445 --> 00:00:16.115
in the special "Gordon Ramsay's
American Road Trip"

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:19.351
airing tomorrow night
at 8:00 p.m., also on Fox.

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:22.021
[ British accent ]
Here is Gordon Ramsay!

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.857
-Mate, it's good to see you,
but happy -- happy New Year.

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:25.991
-[ Normal voice ]
That is so -- thank you.

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:27.493
Happy New Year to you, as well,

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.862
and thank you
for doing this show.

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:32.432
I can't believe that's become
kind of an impression of you.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.267
You don't really even yell
as much anymore.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.936
That's the old impression.
-No, do you know what?

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.905
My kids yell at me more now
than I yell at them,

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.172
so it's the other way around.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.308
-How are the kids?
-Honestly.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.576
Mate, the kids are doing well.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.278
As you know, for everybody,
over the last 12 months,

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:48.381
it's been a -- it's been a tough
sort of, you know, time.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.649
And especially
for those youngsters

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.851
in that age that's sort of,
you know, 16 to 22.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.820
But --
-I couldn't imagine, yeah.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.954
-They're gonna get through.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.189
-But you have five kids now,
right?

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:59.258
-We went back for --
for number five.

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:03.062
-Congratulations, but wow.
-No, but hold on.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.097
Tana's asking
for a sixth across the lockdown

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:06.399
because literally...
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:09.368
...two hours ago,
our prime minister

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.137
has just announced
we're in lockdown now...

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.272
-That's right.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.607
-...until the frickin'
15th of February.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.443
So she said, "We have good news
tomorrow night."

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:18.844
I said, "What's that, darling?"

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:20.580
She said, "Well,
you're up late talking to Jimmy.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.047
Tomorrow night,
we can go for number six."

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:23.916
-[ Laughs ] Oh, my God.
-I said, "Number six?"

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.317
-No! I'm gonna talk to her.
-And then, suddenly --

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:27.286
-I have to talk to her.
No, no, no. It's just not fair.

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.722
-Would you, please?
We do have one little addition.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:30.857
Let me just show you.
-Yeah.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.358
-He arrived literally last fall.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:35.361
This is -- This is Truffle.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.062
Oh, man.
-Oh!

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:38.631
-Hey, Truf--
-Stop it.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.032
[ Laughing ] No, no, no.

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:42.235
Hey, bud! Hi, Truffle!
-Truffle.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.303
-Hi, Truffle.
-Say hello to -- to Uncle Jimmy.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:47.106
-It's Uncle Jimmy.
Truffle, making your TV debut --

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:48.174
oh, and looking good.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.742
Yeah, you know
where the camera is.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.244
He finds the lens.
He finds the lens.

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:54.547
-Oh, my goodness.
-How has he been?

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.316
-Mate, he's been a mess,
and he's sort of --

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:58.417
he's still going through
that process

00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.552
of getting house-trained.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.554
You can always tell
when the dog [bleep]

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.122
'cause the smell rises,

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.824
and even before you open your
bedroom door in the morning,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.292
you think, "Oh, my God."

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.928
It used to be gravy -- now it's
just dog [bleep] you smell.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.596
-[ Laughs ]
-You should see

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:13.399
some of the ridiculous coats
that they've got over here now.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.801
I saw a coat the other day
with his initials,

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.170
his date of birth on it,

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.539
and this thing was dressed
with Christmas tree lights.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.074
-Geez.
-What the [bleep] is happening

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.076
putting Christmas tree lights
on a dog?

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.311
And it went all the way
to the end of the tail.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.647
-I think it's --
-And then I saw this sort of dog

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.148
in the distance,
pissing up a tree...

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.316
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.884
-And it looked
a really weird shape,

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.287
like it was almost like a drone
that had fallen from the sky,

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:37.323
but it's a dog having a [bleep]
and a piss up a tree,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.725
with bloody Christmas tree
lights all over it.

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.961
Sorry.
-You're the first guest in 2021,

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:45.864
and already we're --
NBC is in the hole $20,000.

00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:48.501
-[ Laughs ] Sorry. Sorry.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.736
I'm s-- I'll take care of that.
I'm sorry.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.203
It's you.
You bring the worst out of me.

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:52.671
Last time I saw you, you put me
on the naughty step.

00:02:52.671 --> 00:02:55.875
-I made you sit -- I --
[ Laughs ]

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.843
Dude, I brought -- I made
you sit on the naughty step.

00:02:57.843 --> 00:03:00.113
That's right. I forgot that.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.513
How is the -- How is the --

00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:03.448
What are you feeding the baby,
the 2-year-old?

00:03:03.448 --> 00:03:06.152
I forget those years.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:10.656
-So Oscar, you know, in my mind,
is my last hope

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.224
of getting anyone
into the industry

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:16.796
because, you know, our eldest
daughter is working in PR.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:20.065
Holly, our middle daughter,
is doing fashion.

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:21.467
Tilly's taking a gap year.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.602
Jack has become a Royal Marine.
And so --

00:03:23.602 --> 00:03:25.104
[ Chuckling ]
-What?!

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.372
-Everyone's left --
Everyone's left --

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.340
Everyone's left the nest,
and nobody wants to cook.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.711
So I'm hoping, if we refine
Oscar's palate now...

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.780
-No.
-...he starts off with

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.449
beautiful oatmeal in the morning
with caramelized banana.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.117
I'll do him a little light
scrambled egg on toast

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.251
for lunch.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.352
And then, for dinner tonight,

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:42.121
he had a roasted
butternut squash soup.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.156
[ Both laugh ]
-The kid's spoiled rotten.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:46.292
Are you kidding me? I love that.
-Man.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.559
-But you know that

00:03:47.559 --> 00:03:48.861
no one's gonna take over
the family business.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:51.063
It's just the way life works.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:53.266
-I think they've been watching
too many reruns

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.567
of "Kitchen Nightmares,"
thinking,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.202
"[Bleep] that.
That's not my career."

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.037
-Exactly.
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.572
Hey, Gordon,
I want to talk to you

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.273
about the restaurant business

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:04.010
because I can just imagine
how tough it's been.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.247
You have over 35 restaurants,
I think, all over the world.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.149
-Yeah.
-What it's been like?

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.751
I try to support --
whenever I can --

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.319
I have been ordering every week,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:16.022
at least three nights a week
of take-out.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.825
And even if I'm not hungry,
I freeze it, just --

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.360
and give them a nice, big tip.
-Sure.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.862
-But what's it been like, bud?
-Sure.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.597
Yeah, I mean, unprecedented.
-Terrible.

00:04:25.597 --> 00:04:28.501
-I've never seen a situation
like this, ever.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.403
London, like New York,
has been hit really hard.

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:36.308
I think the biggest, you know,
and most important thing for me

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:40.112
is staying close to the staff,
giving them the security,

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:43.348
giving them, you know,
light at the end of the tunnel,

00:04:43.348 --> 00:04:45.218
holding regular calls.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:48.354
If we don't meet, you know,
on a Zoom or jump on the phone

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.856
three or four times a day,

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.959
and for that younger bracket,
the ones that are under 30,

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.828
it's really important
to keep their mind focused

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.830
that we are going to
come out of this.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.098
Customers have been amazing,

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.566
supporting the restaurants
with to-go,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:05.337
and, you know, special festive
menus, which has been amazing.

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:07.440
Some of the landlords
have been really supportive

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.941
and some haven't.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.876
-So we're
in that awkward situation,

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:13.012
no different to theaters.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.914
You know, breaking bread
and having that social connect

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:18.251
is absolutely pivotal.

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:21.053
So we are
going to come out of this.

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:23.322
You've got to stand strong,
hold your nerve,

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:26.826
and, more importantly,
keep these youngsters on-site

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.861
and give them hope,
and that's what we're doing.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.929
-You're been on TV --
I was reading this,

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:31.964
and I find this
hard to believe --

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.700
for 20 years now,
over 20 years.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.068
That's crazy.

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:37.636
I remembered when you were,
like, a brand-new thing

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:38.905
I thought I discovered.

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.440
And I go, "[Gasps]
I just found the coolest guy.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.007
He's crazy, man.
He's blah, blah, blah."

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:43.910
-Yeah.
-But what went through your mind

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.577
when you were first asked
to do a show?

00:05:45.577 --> 00:05:47.446
I think I know the answer.

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:49.248
I think you were like,
"No, I'm not a TV chef.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:52.317
I'm a chef, chef."
-That's -- That's exactly that.

00:05:52.317 --> 00:05:53.652
And it's weird because

00:05:53.652 --> 00:05:56.588
I felt that someone was trying
to sort of ruin my career

00:05:56.588 --> 00:05:58.557
by taking me
out of that level of perfection.

00:05:58.557 --> 00:06:00.226
And so,
the first thing I said --

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.694
"Look,
will I be back before 6:30

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.629
so I can get behind the line
and start,

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.031
you know, cooking for
the first table at 6:45?"

00:06:06.031 --> 00:06:08.267
-Wow.
-And this -- this year,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.468
Restaurant Gordon Ramsay
in Chelsea --

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:11.237
we celebrate 22 years,

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:14.106
and TV came literally
two years after opening.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:19.344
So I said to the producer --
I said, "Look, I'm a real chef."

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:21.246
"No, no,
but you can cook on TV."

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:22.581
I said,
"No, I don't want to cook on TV

00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:23.683
because you're never gonna --

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:24.983
you're not gonna show
the passion."

00:06:24.983 --> 00:06:26.886
Said, "No, no, trust me.
We'll show the passion."

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:30.690
So, you know,
the first-ever sort of time

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.659
is when I launched
this tiny, little documentary

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.927
called "Kitchen Nightmares."

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:38.330
One cameraman, one producer,
one sound, and myself --

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.565
there was four of us.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.200
And I used to go
and spend two weeks

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.136
in these restaurants
per restaurant with the owners

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:45.772
and then go back a month later

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:47.606
and spend
a further three or four days,

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:49.608
and everything I was learning
in the industry

00:06:49.608 --> 00:06:51.277
after opening my first business

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:54.113
I was putting into
these restaurants.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:57.249
And of course, you know, I was
desperate for them to succeed.

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:59.752
And that was the first thing
that sort of hit me --

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:01.920
the devastation --
if it didn't work,

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.057
I felt that I was the one
that they were going to blame.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:07.025
So I give it my all, man.
I tell you.

00:07:07.025 --> 00:07:08.127
Oh, my God.
-Yeah.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.862
I want to talk to you more about
the shows

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:11.297
you have premiering this week
when we come back.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:12.898
Is that cool?
-Absolutely.

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:14.667
-More with Gordon Ramsay
when we come back, everybody.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.701
Stick around.
Come on back.

